  "metaDescription": "Authorities are investigating a fatal explosion at an oil refinery in Cepu, Blora, which reportedly occurred while workers were managing empty tanks.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "One worker died from injuries after an explosion occurred at an oil refinery facility in Cepu, Blora.",
    "The Ministry of Energy and Mineral Resources is currently conducting an investigation into the cause of the incident.",
    "Preliminary reports suggest the explosion may have been triggered by residual gas trapped inside an empty storage tank."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "A fatal explosion took place at a facility operated by the Human Resource Development Center for Oil and Gas (PPSDM Migas) in Cepu, Blora, Central Java. The site, which is primarily utilized for vocational training and competence testing rather than commercial production, experienced a sudden blast that resulted in the death of one worker who suffered severe burns. The Ministry of Energy and Mineral Resources (ESDM) has launched a formal investigation to determine the precise circumstances leading to the incident. Initial findings from official sources indicate that the blast may have been caused by residual gas remaining within a tank previously believed to be empty. Local government officials are separately addressing regional interests regarding oil and gas management as investigations into site safety protocols continue alongside the official inquiry into the industrial accident.",
